- [Contributing](#contributing)\
- [License](#license)\
- [Acknowledgments](#acknowledgments)\
\
## Features\
\
- **Automatic Language Detection and Transcription**: Utilizes the Whisper AI model to automatically detect the language of the audio and transcribe speech to text with high accuracy.\
- **Subtitle Timing**: Generates precise timestamps for each subtitle segment, formatted in the standard .srt format.\
- **User-Friendly GUI**: Built with Tkinter, the script provides an intuitive graphical interface, making it easy for users to select audio files, choose model types, and manage the transcription process.\
- **GPU Acceleration**: Supports CUDA-enabled GPUs to accelerate the transcription process using PyTorch, reducing processing time significantly for large audio files.\
- **Customizable Accuracy and Speed**: Offers multiple Whisper model sizes (tiny, base, small, medium, large) to balance between accuracy and processing speed based on user needs.\
- **Real-Time Status Updates**: Displays real-time progress and allows users to cancel the transcription process if needed.\
\
## Installation\
\
To set up the AI-Based Subtitle Generation Script on your local machine, follow these steps:\
\
### Prerequisites\
\
- Python 3.x installed on your system. Download it from [Python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).\
\
### Clone the Repository\
\
1. Clone the repository to your local machine using Git:\
   ```bash\
   git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ai-subtitle-generator.git\
   cd ai-subtitle-generator\
   ```\
\
### Install Required Dependencies\
\
2. Install the necessary Python packages. It is recommended to use a virtual environment:\
\
   ```bash\
   pip install torch tkinter pillow openai-whisper\
   ```\
\
### Install PyTorch\
\
3. Follow the instructions on the [PyTorch website](https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/) to install the appropriate version of PyTorch for your system.\
\
## Usage\
\
To use the AI-Based Subtitle Generation Script, follow these steps:\
\
### Running the Script\
\
1. Navigate to the project directory:\
   ```bash\
   cd ai-subtitle-generator\
   ```\
\
2. Run the script:\
   ```bash\
   python subtitle_generator.py\
   ```\
\
### Using the GUI\
\
- **Select an Audio File**: Click "Browse" to choose the audio file you wish to transcribe. Supported formats include MP3, WAV, and M4A.\
- **Choose Model Type**: Select a Whisper model type from the dropdown menu based on your requirements for speed and accuracy.\
- **Set Output Path**: Specify where the generated .srt subtitle file should be saved.\
- **Start Transcription**: Click "Process" to begin the transcription. The progress bar will indicate the status of the transcription process.\
- **Cancel Transcription**: If necessary, click "Cancel" to stop the transcription process.\
- **View Help**: Click "Help" for detailed instructions on how to use the script.\
\
## GUI Overview\
\
The script features a graphical user interface (GUI) designed for ease of use:\
\
- **Audio File Selection**: A text entry field and "Browse" button to select the audio file.\
- **SRT File Save Location**: A text entry field and "Save As" button to specify the output path for the .srt file.\
- **Model Selection Dropdown**: A combo box to select the Whisper model size (tiny, base, small, medium, large).\
- **Progress Bar**: Shows the progress of the transcription process.\
- **Status Label**: Displays the current status of the transcription process.\
- **Control Buttons**: Buttons to start, cancel, and access help information for the transcription process.\
\
## Model Selection Guide\
\
The Whisper AI model provides several options to balance between speed and accuracy:\
\
- **Tiny**: Fastest model, less accurate. Suitable for quick, rough transcriptions.\
- **Base**: Good balance between speed and accuracy for general use.\
- **Small**: Offers higher accuracy with moderate processing time.\
- **Medium**: Higher accuracy, requires more processing power and time.\
- **Large**: Most accurate, but slowest. Requires a powerful system, ideally with a CUDA-enabled GPU for faster processing.\
\
**Recommendation**: Use the "large" model for the highest accuracy, especially for long or complex audio files, if you have the necessary hardware resources.\
